                <note rend="inline" type="source">791.5622/8–1452</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Military
                        Assistance in the Department of Defense</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Olmsted</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State’s Special Assistant for Mutual
                        Security Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Martin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-08-14">August 14, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Reimbursable Military Assistance Under Section 408(<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >e</hi>) of the MDAA, as Amended—Case
                        No. OMA India 7</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Reference is made to your memorandum, subject as above, dated <pb
                            facs="0612" n="1662" xml:id="pg1662"/> 13 May 1952, which forwarded note
                        from the Indian Embassy requesting procurement of fighter aircraft for the
                        Indian Government.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In accordance with oral requests made by your office, the estimated
                        pricing and availability study made by the Department of the Air Force on
                        the 54 C–119 aircraft requested under this
                        case is forwarded for information and study.</item>
                </list>
